---
import RoomMock from './mocks/RoomMock.astro'
---

  <section class="feat rev" id="together">
    <div class="wrap feat-in">
      <div class="feat-copy" data-reveal>
        <h2>Two machines, one timeline</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Share a six-character code and everyone in the room stays on the same position, pauses and episode. Seek on one and the other lands on the same frame, even on a slow connection.
        </p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Drift is corrected by speed, not by seeking</b> — ten seconds at 103% closes the gap without a jump.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>The room waits for whoever is buffering</b> and resumes by itself.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Torrents need no pasting:</b> everyone joins the same swarm. Only the timeline goes through the relay, never the video.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <a class="more-link" href="/watch-together">How watching together works</a>
      </div>
      <div class="feat-mock" data-reveal style="--dl:1">
        <RoomMock />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
